# UI

Read `docs/design-language.md` before changing a screen. That file holds the tokens. A mock loses if it conflicts with the file.

- Use only colors, type, and motion named there. If a value is missing, add it to the doc after the user chooses it. Do not ship an invented palette as the brand.
- Near-black and off-white are a direction, not a license to pick final hex values.
- Black mark on light grounds. White mark on black grounds. Do not recolor the logo.
- After the intro, pages stay quiet: no stars, nebulae, glow, decorative gradients, or neon.
- Mobile and desktop are both real layouts. Same tasks. Stacked on a phone, more air and a stricter grid on a wide screen.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` disables autoplay and non-essential motion. The intro uses its still frame. Write that with Tailwind's `motion-reduce:` variant.
- Checkout is Shopify's page. Do not rebuild it.
- Style with Tailwind utility classes, as decided in `docs/architecture.md`. The Tailwind entry file is the only handwritten CSS. Do not add a CSS module or a per-component stylesheet.
- `docs/design-language.md` and the accepted requirement win over `design-taste-frontend` and over any third-party `DESIGN.md`.

```tsx
// Wrong: an unnamed palette treated as final
<button className="bg-[#111111] font-[Neue Haas Grotesk]">Add</button>

// Right: a token that already exists in docs/design-language.md
<button className="bg-ground text-paper motion-reduce:transition-none">Add</button>
```
